Message-ID: <1tu88f$kpr@elxr.jpl.nasa.gov>

st10t@Rosie.UH.EDU writes:
>	(1) The user shall not seek or reveal information on, obtain copies of,
>	or modify files, tapes or passwords belonging to other users, nor may
>	the user misrepresent others.  The user may only use his/her legal name
>	or actual title at the University.  Only one person may use a computer
>	account, and that is the person to whom the account was granted.

So "ls" is illegal to do outside of one own's home directory. Further, if 
the "path" variable contains "/bin", then you have also violated this statute...
given that a hash table is made in your shell by the act of logging in that
contains information on files belonging to other users.

>	(6) The user shall not engage in behavior that creates an unpleasant
>	environment for other users.

Like failing to wear underarm deodorant? Or talking too loud? Hmmm...

>   violations of these conditions are unethical and may be violations of 
>University policy and/or criminal offenses.  

So, it's against policy to forget to wear underarm deodorant. Interesting.

These policies suck. If I were a thinking about being a student there, if I
saw these policies I wouldn't be. 
